  displayName: Grey whale
  scientificName: Eschrichtius robustus
  description: One of the largest animals found along the Pacific coast, the gray
    whale is known for its long annual migrations between Arctic feeding grounds
    and warmer breeding waters. Its mottled gray skin is often marked by barnacles
    and scars accumulated throughout its life.
  depthLayer: 
  behavior: Moves slowly and deliberately through the environment, often following
    a steady course. Occasionally surfaces to breathe before descending.
